# Utility Functions - MCP Platform Integration

## Implementation Patterns for System Context Functions

### Overview
When implementing utility functions that need system information, always leverage existing MCP tools and platform APIs instead of creating redundant implementations.

### Key Files and Modules

#### Core Utility Module
- [src-tauri/src/utils/mod.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/utils/mod.rs) - Main utility functions including system context gathering

#### MCP Platform APIs
- [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/engine.rs](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/engine.rs) - NSWorkspace functionality
- [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/element.rs](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/element.rs) - Element detection and focused element APIs
- [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/utils.rs](mdc:src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/macos/utils.rs) - Screenshot capture and display utilities

