## Common Patterns

### 1. Finding Existing Implementations
- Search for similar functionality in MCP tools first
- Check platform-specific modules for OS APIs
- Look for NSWorkspace usage patterns in existing code

### 2. Avoiding Redundancy
- Use existing screenshot capture instead of new display APIs
- Leverage established objc messaging patterns
- Reuse existing error handling approaches

### 3. Platform Compatibility
```rust
#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
{
    // macOS-specific implementation using MCP tools
}

#[cfg(not(target_os = "macos"))]
{
    // Fallback or unsupported platform handling
}
```

This rule ensures utility functions integrate seamlessly with the existing MCP platform architecture while avoiding code duplication.
